1
00:00:02,287 --> 00:00:10,516
Marketing & Consent
Plan campaigns, reach only clients who agreed to it, and measure what each campaign brings in.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,640
Emilie plans a first-home campaign for young professionals
Growth ▸ Marketing & Consent

3
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:40,280
Sign in as Emilie Fanchette — Marketing Executive
Marketing Executive — plans and runs campaigns

4
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:52,600
A segment describes the audience: who should hear about the offer
Existing segments: HNW without a mandate, FMB 2029 holders, Francophone affluent…

5
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,960
The criteria are a filter over the client master
Build the matching list with the same filter in Reports

6
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:08,200
New campaign: objective, product, channels, audience
It starts in Planning

7
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:15,120
Budget and dates — the budget is the cost ROI is measured against
Actual cost is entered when the invoices come in

8
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:22,440
The tracking code goes into every website link of the campaign
An enquiry arriving through such a link is credited to this campaign

9
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:32,200
Add the clients who will receive it
Marketing & Consent ▸ Campaign Members ▸ New

10
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,480
Deepak Seegoolam has given marketing consent — accepted

11
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:43,400
Now Corinne Henry…
A client with a complaint that is still open

12
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:51,600
Refused: the client is suppressed from marketing
No consent, “do not contact”, or an open complaint — the CRM never lets these through

13
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:58,440
A campaign is a financial promotion
Compliance signs it off before it can be approved or go live

14
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:03,080
Try to approve it straight away…

15
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:11,760
Blocked: Compliance must sign it off first
Move it to Compliance review instead

16
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:20,560
Compliance review: the sign-off request is now in Compliance's Approvals inbox
Segment, budget, dates and the message must be filled before this move

17
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:25,880
Fatima checks the message and approves it
Tools ▸ Approvals — the requester can never approve her own campaign

18
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:30,160
Sign in as Fatima Hossenbux — Compliance Officer
Compliance Officer — signs off marketing material

19
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:41,440
The request shows the budget, the dates and the message
Open the record to review it, comment, then Approve or Reject

20
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:47,600
Approved: the campaign moves to Approved by itself
Rejecting it would send it back to Planning with the comment

21
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,800
Emilie launches the campaign
She is told it was approved

22
00:02:51,800 --> 00:03:08,800
Sign in as Emilie Fanchette — Marketing Executive
Marketing Executive

23
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:15,280
Live: the emails and the social posts go out
Each member's sent date, opens and responses are tracked

24
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:33,634
Kevin Rampersad clicks the campaign ad
The link opens the website enquiry form with the campaign's tracking code

25
00:03:33,634 --> 00:03:40,491
Sent — he has a reference number and his consent to be contacted is recorded

26
00:03:40,491 --> 00:03:49,051
The enquiry kept the tracking code and is credited to the campaign
Routing and scoring work as for any enquiry — the Lending team calls him back

27
00:03:49,051 --> 00:04:00,451
Across campaigns: budget, audience, enquiries, revenue and ROI
Home loans Q3 earned more than it cost; a negative ROI means no revenue yet

28
00:04:00,451 --> 00:04:07,611
Our campaign: its audience and 1 attributed enquiry
Loans that follow and their revenue roll up here too — that is what ROI is measured on

29
00:04:07,611 --> 00:04:21,611
A seminar for the campaign's audience
Events & Seminars ▸ New

30
00:04:21,611 --> 00:04:25,222
Guests register — from the website or added by staff
Event Registrations ▸ Register guest

31
00:04:25,222 --> 00:04:35,621
On the evening, Shamim Noël attends — tick Attended
Her relationship manager is told to follow up

32
00:04:35,621 --> 00:04:39,701
The event counts registrations, attendance and the attendance rate

33
00:04:39,701 --> 00:04:49,461
At the event Shamim asks for the research notes
Newsletter & Research Subscriptions ▸ New

34
00:04:49,461 --> 00:04:54,701
Subscribers of a topic receive each publication when it is sent
“Send to subscribers” on a research note emails them in their language

35
00:04:54,701 --> 00:04:58,861
Priya, her RM, was notified to follow up
Signed in as the relationship manager

36
00:04:58,861 --> 00:05:04,092
Sign in as Priya Ramdin — Relationship Manager
Relationship Manager — follows up event guests

37
00:05:04,092 --> 00:05:09,913
She calls to thank her and records the follow-up
Tick “Follow-up done” on the registration

38
00:05:09,913 --> 00:05:17,725
On the call Shamim says: no more marketing, please
Open her marketing consent and record the withdrawal

39
00:05:17,725 --> 00:05:23,325
Marketing consent: No — she is now suppressed from marketing
The withdrawal takes effect at once, as in the Clients tutorial

40
00:05:23,325 --> 00:05:27,485
Emilie tries to add Shamim Noël to the campaign
Signed in as Marketing

41
00:05:27,485 --> 00:05:39,725
Sign in as Emilie Fanchette — Marketing Executive
Marketing Executive

42
00:05:39,725 --> 00:05:44,765
Refused — she withdrew her consent
Research mailings sent to subscribers skip her too

43
00:05:44,765 --> 00:06:00,285
The Marketing dashboard sums it all up
Live campaigns, attributed enquiries, attendance, subscribers, ROI

44
00:06:00,285 --> 00:06:06,563
ROI and attributed revenue by campaign, engagement, subscriptions by topic

45
00:06:06,563 --> 00:06:16,765
Marketing & Consent
Campaigns reach only clients who agreed, and every result is credited back to them.
